    "image_with_text_YFy6rM": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_4W4pwU": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Yahrzeit Candles for Remembrance",
            "subheading_tag": "h2",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "border_Lyk3P4": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "text_G7eEn9": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The Yahrzeit candle, also called a Ner Neshama, meaning \"candle of the soul,\" symbolizes the soul's enduring presence. It's lit at home, sometimes in a synagogue, and in some families in front of a photograph or memorial space dedicated to the person being remembered.</p><p>Most people light a single Yahrzeit candle for each person they are observing. Families with multiple losses sometimes light several candles together. The candle is generally lit just before sundown at the start of the Hebrew calendar date and left to burn out naturally.<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        },
        "subheading_ch9Rq4": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Yahrzeit Candles for Remembrance",
            "subheading_tag": "h2",
            "subheading_font_class": "fs-heading-5-base"
          }
        },
        "border_7FLkyj": {
          "type": "border",
          "settings": {}
        },
        "text_iERUX7": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The most commonly chosen format is a glass-contained memorial candle designed to burn for about 24 hours. The glass container serves two purposes: it keeps the wax fully contained during the long burn and provides a stable base that doesn't require a separate holder.</p><p>When choosing, the main practical questions are burn time and quantity. If you observe multiple Yahrzeits throughout the year for parents, siblings, or other family members, ordering a multipack keeps you prepared without having to source them one at a time. For community or synagogue use, bulk Yahrzeit candles options are available to cover a full congregation's needs across the Jewish calendar.<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_font_class": "fs-body-75"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "subheading_4W4pwU",
        "border_Lyk3P4",
        "text_G7eEn9",
        "subheading_ch9Rq4",
        "border_7FLkyj",
        "text_iERUX7"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
