    "collapsible_row_list_r7Akeg": {
      "type": "collapsible-row-list",
      "blocks": {
        "item_bkFRMA": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How long does a Yahrzeit candle burn?",
            "text": "<p>Yahrzeit candles are typically designed to burn for approximately 24 to 26 hours. This allows the candle to remain lit from the start of the Hebrew calendar date at sundown through the following evening. Exact burn time can vary slightly depending on the specific candle format and placement conditions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_89daVr": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "When do I light a Yahrzeit candle?",
            "text": "<p>The traditional practice is to light the Yahrzeit candle before sundown at the start of the Hebrew calendar date of the person's passing. If you're unsure of the Hebrew date, many Jewish calendars available in print and online provide a conversion tool from the secular date.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "item_87km6Q": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How many Yahrzeit candles should I light?",
            "text": "<p>The standard practice is one candle per person being remembered. Families observing multiple Yahrzeits at the same time sometimes light one candle for each person. There is no strict rule on the number, family and community custom tends to guide this.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_bLjGe8": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What surface should I place a Yahrzeit candle on?",
            "text": "<p>A flat, stable, heat-safe surface is the practical starting point. Ceramic tile, a metal tray, or a stone surface works well. Avoid placing glass memorial candles directly on finished wood, as the heat from the glass can leave marks over a long burn.<br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "item_RURrMN": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I leave a Yahrzeit candle unattended?",
            "text": "<p>Yahrzeit candles are traditionally left to burn throughout the full observance period, meaning they burn unattended for significant portions of that time. Using a glass container for a candle on a heat-safe surface, in a location away from flammable materials and drafts, is the standard safe setup. Standard fire safety practices apply.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_NwTNbR": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Are Yahrzeit candles unscented?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Jewish Yahrzeit candles used for religious observance are unscented. This is consistent with the broader practice of keeping Jewish ritual candles fragrance-free.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_UCyEVK": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Do you sell Yahrzeit candles in bulk for synagogues?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Bulk and wholesale pricing is available for synagogues, Jewish community centers, and other organizations. Contact us with your anticipated quantity and timing, and we'll work out a purchasing arrangement that fits your needs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_MgRhaD": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I use a regular candle for Yahrzeit instead?",
            "text": "<p>A standard household candle is not an ideal substitute because it won't match the 24-hour burn expectation. A Yahrzeit candle in the appropriate format ensures the candle burns for the full observance window without needing to be replaced during the day.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
